@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static account UI. Open `index.html` through your static hosting setup. No build or runtime dependencies are required. The site intentionally defaults to a **preview account**, labeled in the UI. Sample passkeys persist in browser local storage, and preview actions never invoke authenticator synchronization.
+
+## Live account integration
+
+This repository has no authentication server, credential database, or passkey registration flow. To connect an existing account backend, add this to the HTML head:
+
+```html
+<meta name="passkey-api" content="/api/account/passkeys">
+```
+
+The same-origin API must authenticate the signed-in customer using its session and scope every read and mutation to that customer. Return `401` for an expired session. Mutations must validate the CSRF token, request origin, ownership, and the trimmed name (1–60 characters). Do not trust record IDs as authorization. Never return private credential material. Use HTTPS and `Cache-Control: no-store` on responses.
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: return the complete authenticated snapshot below, without pagination or filtering.
+- `PATCH /api/account/passkeys/:id`: accept `{ "name": "Work laptop" }` and return the updated complete snapshot.
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: revoke the credential for authentication, then return the complete updated snapshot, including an empty list after the last deletion. Do not return `204`.
+- Both mutations receive `X-CSRF-Token` from the latest snapshot. Return `409` for conflicts.
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "your-site.example",
+  "userId": "BASE64URL_WEBAUTHN_USER_HANDLE",
+  "csrfToken": "SESSION_BOUND_CSRF_TOKEN",
+  "passkeys": [
+    {
+      "id": "opaque-database-record-id",
+      "credentialId": "BASE64URL_CREDENTIAL_ID",
+      "name": "MacBook Air",
+      "device": "laptop",
+      "provider": "iCloud Keychain",
+      "createdAt": "2026-10-12T09:00:00Z",
+      "lastUsedAt": "2026-11-08T09:00:00Z",
+      "current": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+`userId` is the base64url-encoded WebAuthn user handle, not a database user ID. `credentialId` is the base64url WebAuthn credential ID. `id` is the API's record identifier. Supported device icons are `laptop`, `phone`, and `usb`; unknown devices use a key icon. `current` means the credential used for this session. Metadata fields are optional.
+
+Live mode never falls back to sample data on an API failure. On authenticated load and after a committed deletion, the client prefers `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` with the complete list. Deletion falls back to `signalUnknownCredential` when needed. Browser support is detected; rejected signals offer retry and manual password-manager instructions. A successful signal is a request to the authenticator, not proof every device has updated. Renaming only changes the account's passkey label; WebAuthn's `signalCurrentUserDetails` changes a user's identity details and is deliberately not used for per-key labels. See the [WebAuthn signal specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn/#sctn-signalAllAcceptedCredentials).
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/passkeys.test.mjs
+node --input-type=module --check < account.js
+```
+
+No browser checks, development servers, preview servers, or server entrypoint imports are needed for these checks.
